# harness: machine-local and cache files
.harness/env.local
.harness/board.sqlite
.harness/board.sqlite.tmp
__pycache__/
*.pyc
board.html

# The board of this repository, and every document that the board produces.
# This repository is the harness. The work that we do WITH the harness is not the
# harness, so git tracks the tool and never the dogfood. `python3 -m harness init`
# writes every file below again from its template, and `session open` does it for
# you when it finds them missing. `.harness/manifest.json` stays in git: it carries
# the checksums that prove that this repository still hosts itself.
work/sprints/*
!work/sprints/.gitkeep
# sprint-000 is the exception, and it ships. It is the setup sprint of this
# repository, and it is the only worked example of a real sprint that a reader can
# open: a sprint sheet, an epic sheet, and the four state folders. Every later
# sprint is the work that we do with the harness, and it stays local.
!work/sprints/sprint-000/
# The task file of sprint-000 stays out of git. The folder shape ships, and the
# progress does not. A move of TASK-0001 between state folders is the work that we do
# with the harness, and law 1 says that the folder tree is the truth. An adopter gets
# the same task from `harness/templates/work/backlog/TASK-0001-*.md`, which the package
# carries and `init` writes into the backlog.
work/sprints/sprint-000/**/TASK-*.md
work/backlog/TASK-*.md
work/ROADMAP.md
docs/sessions/*.md
docs/ACTIVITY.md
docs/session-log.md
.harness/journal.jsonl
.harness/escalations.md
.harness/targets.json
